                "evidence": "**I couldn't find any evidence of what people regret about moving to Tailwind v5.** The only thing I found is the official announcement, so anything I said about regrets would be a guess.\n\n**What the sources say**\n- Tailwind v5 was released on 2026-08-20 ([official announcement](https://tailwindcss.com/blog/tailwindcss-v5)). I read the whole page.\n- CSS-first configuration is now the default, and the JavaScript config file (`tailwind.config.js`) has been removed.\n- There are new container query defaults.\n- The engine is now Lightning CSS.\n- The migration tool is `npx @tailwindcss/upgrade@5`.\n\n**What I didn't find**\n- The vault had no pages on Tailwind.\n- Three web searches (Exa and Tavily) returned no migration write-ups, GitHub issues, forum threads or retrospectives. Every result was the announcement itself.\n- The social lane is missing. The `last30days` skill isn't installed here, and that is the tool meant for practitioner opinion and regrets. I didn't imitate it with extra web searches.\n\n**My own inference (not from a source)**\nThe removal of the JS config is the change most likely to cause friction. Projects that rely on `tailwind.config.js` for plugins, dynamic theme values or shared presets would have the most to rewrite. The announcement doesn't say how much of that the upgrade tool handles, so treat this as a lead to check, not a finding.\n\n**Ways to get a real answer**\n- Search the `tailwindlabs/tailwindcss` GitHub issues, filtered to issues opened since August 2026, for upgrade-tool failures.\n- Search r/tailwindcss and Hacker News threads on the v5 release.\n- Install `last30days` and I'll rerun this with the social lane.\n\nI didn't write to the vault, because the only new fact is the announcement. I can save it as a short page if you want.\n\n**Coverage:** vault searched (no matches). Exa and Tavily searched (announcement only). Firecrawl for GitHub issues wasn't tried. Social lane missing (`last30days` not installed). No paid calls beyond the provider searches."
              }
